ms-a2-fancontrol (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Crash or error sets the emergency level instead of the firmware levels;
    only a regular stop restores them (ExecStopPost "stop-post" reads
    SERVICE_RESULT). After a restart the levels fall gradually from the
    current EC values.

 -- ProxForge <ms-a2-fancontrol@proxforge.invalid>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:15:00 +0100

ms-a2-fancontrol (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Emergency level: both fans to full speed (level 60) at NVMe 70 C,
    controller sensor 85 C, RAM 68 C, CPU 92 C or without temperatures.
  * Serialize EC port access with a lock file, so "status" cannot
    interleave with the running service.

 -- ProxForge <ms-a2-fancontrol@proxforge.invalid>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0100

